# ROWNAA — Phase 6: Mobile CSS (App Experience) & QA

> Mobile CSS is a completely separate file. The mobile experience must feel like a native app. No shrunk-down website. Read Phase 0 CSS Architecture before writing any mobile styles.

---

## 1. Mobile CSS File Rule (ABSOLUTE)

- File: `/styles/mobile.css` and `/styles/admin-mobile.css`
- Loaded only via: `<link media="screen and (max-width: 768px)">`
- Must NEVER contain `min-width` media queries
- Must NEVER reference desktop-only classes
- All pixel values, padding, margin, font-size defined independently (do NOT inherit from desktop.css via cascade assumptions)

---

## 2. Global Mobile Layout (mobile.css)

### Body & Root
```css
body {
  background-color: var(--color-brand-primary);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--text-body);     /* 15px on mobile */
  overscroll-behavior: none;       /* Prevents browser pull-to-refresh */
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

/* Prevent horizontal scroll globally */
html, body {
  overflow-x: hidden;
  width: 100%;
}

/* Safe area padding for notched phones (iPhone X+) */
.page-wrapper {
  padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);
}
```

---

## 3. Mobile Navigation (Replaces Desktop Top Navbar Entirely)

### Customer Site — Mobile Navbar
- **Top bar (fixed, 56px height):**
  - Left: Hamburger icon (if needed) OR back arrow (on inner pages)
  - Center: "ROWNAA" logo text
  - Right: Notification bell + User avatar (32px circle)
  - Background: `var(--color-brand-primary)`, `border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07)`

- **Bottom Navigation Bar (fixed, 60px + safe-area height):**
  - Position: `fixed; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; z-index: 1000`
  - Background: `var(--color-brand-secondary)` with top border `1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07)`
  - 4 items: Home (house icon) | Book (plus-circle) | Bookings (calendar) | Profile (user)
  - Each item: icon (24px) + label text (10px) below, stacked vertically
  - Active: icon + label → `var(--color-brand-accent)` color
  - Touch target for each item: minimum 44px × 56px
  - `padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` applied to the bar itself

### Admin & Owner Panel — Mobile Bottom Nav
- **Owner:** Dashboard | Bookings | My Cars | Earnings | Profile (5 items)
- **Admin:** Dashboard | Registrations | Bookings | Payments | More (5th opens bottom sheet)
- Same styling rules as customer nav

---

## 4. Bottom Sheets (Replace All Modals & Overlays)

**All popups, filter panels, and forms on mobile open as slide-up bottom sheets — NOT centered modal dialogs.**

### Bottom Sheet Structure
```
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│    ▬  (drag handle bar)    │ ← 4px wide, 40px long, rounded, centered
│                             │
│   Sheet Content             │
│                             │
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

### Bottom Sheet CSS Properties
```css
.bottom-sheet {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  background: var(--color-brand-secondary);
  border-radius: 20px 20px 0 0;
  padding: 12px 20px 0;
  max-height: 90vh;
  overflow-y: auto;
  transform: translateY(100%);
  transition: transform 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  z-index: 2000;
}

.bottom-sheet.open {
  transform: translateY(0);
}

.bottom-sheet-overlay {
  position: fixed; inset: 0;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
  z-index: 1999;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.bottom-sheet-overlay.visible {
  opacity: 1;
  pointer-events: all;
}
```

**When to use bottom sheets on mobile:**
- All filter panels (booking filters, car listing filters)
- All form dialogs (End Trip modal, confirm booking modal)
- All action menus (car card actions, booking actions)
- Map area picker
- Service selector on homepage

---

